{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nwi5RYP9Frf8qYhVbuLF5Z","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental NMR temperature dependence Murday Cotts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy\",\"url\":\"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"ecs.confex.com\",\"url\":\"https://ecs.confex.com/ecs/imlb2016/webprogram/Paper76763.html\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"link.aps.org\",\"url\":\"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.83.094302\"},{\"title\":\"Study of transport processes in Li-ion electrolytes by Multi-nuclear diffusion NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/2020/09/21/study-of-transport-processes-in-li-ion-electrolytes-by-multi-nuclear-diffusion-nmr/\"},{\"title\":\"next.sciencegate.app\",\"url\":\"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517\"}]\n\nI found the Murday and Cotts reference, but not their actual coefficients or temperature fit, so the search doesn't answer your question directly.\n\n- **The paper itself:** Murday and Cotts' 1968 paper, \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" appears in a reference list as J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945 Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945. A separate abstract, likely from the same work, reports that the coefficient of self-diffusion of 7Li in liquid lithium has been measured with nuclear magnetic resonance, determined from the dependence of the spin-echo signal upon the amplitude of a pulsed magnetic field gradient. That abstract also says the results were compared with the Cohen–Turnbull free-volume model and the Ascarelli–Paskin dense-gas model. I could not confirm that this abstract belongs to the 1968 paper.\n- **Later comparisons:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study reports that calculated self-diffusion coefficient is in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere. It also notes that little liquid lithium experimental self-diffusion coefficient were reported in the literature, and that its simulations give an Arrhenius-type fit (the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results).\n- **Other experiments:** Feinauer, Majer and Seeger published experimental data on 6Li and 7Li diffusivities in 1994.\n- **Not applicable:** A Springer paper gives a diffusion expression with D10=0.038 cm2s−1, Q1=12.0 kcal mol−1, but it concerns solid lithium, so it should not be used for the liquid.\n\nTo get the Murday and Cotts numbers, you would need the 1968 paper itself, which these results don't include.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ef7a94b-5815-4eed-b3e5-83caf938b21c","uuid":"9350808d-744f-47b0-9ec1-18fb48c7bd09","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:37:33.861Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient experimental NMR temperature dependence Murday Cotts","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011q9f6eqVVqzKvGSvC9m2wD","content":[{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy","url":"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR","url":"