notes that little liquid lithium experimental self-diffusion coefficient were reported in the literature, and that its simulations give an Arrhenius-type fit (the Arrhenius equation according to the simulation results).\n- **Other experiments:** Feinauer, Majer and Seeger published experimental data on 6Li and 7Li diffusivities in 1994.\n- **Not applicable:** A Springer paper gives a diffusion expression with D10=0.038 cm2s−1, Q1=12.0 kcal mol−1, but it concerns solid lithium, so it should not be used for the liquid.\n\nTo get the Murday and Cotts numbers, you would need the 1968 paper itself, which these results don't include."],"durationSeconds":7.3944350290000145,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nwi5RYP9Frf8qYhVbuLF5Z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
